.SH NAME
cw \- cw move
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cw
\fI\,move \/\fR[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,TARGET\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IP
Move the current tab to a Context/Window.
.IP
Creates the Context and/or Window if they don't exist (asks first).
.IP
Examples:
.TP
cw move MyProject/Dev
move tab to window "Dev" in "MyProject"
.TP
cw move NewProject/Main
creates both if needed
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
